          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Smart Action Selection"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768478988499"
          },
          "code": "SMART_ACTION_SELECTION",
          "id": "1761744388723",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1761744388725_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a text analyzer, the goal is to detect the invalid input text values and to follow the next instructions.\n\nYou will receive a JSON object with the following properties:\n- `SRNumber`: the identifier of the service request\n- `message`: the user's message or intent\n- `actions`: a list of actions, each with metadata\n\nThis is an `input message` sample:\n```json\n{\n\"SRNumber\": \"SR0000070663\",\n\"message\": \"I want to transfer this SR to another person\",\n\"actions\": [\n{\n\"DisplayLabel\": \"Add Action\",\n\"UserActionName\": \"SDA-ExecuteAction-serviceRequests\"\n}\n]\n}\n```\n\n*INSTRUCTIONS*\n\n#Use this input text:\n<inputText>\n {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n</inputText>\n\n1. Use **ONLY**  the `message` JSON property of the provided `inputText` for  the invalid words removal. Follow these rules to detect the invalid words:\n\n#Invalid text detection **Rules**\n- The input text should have at least two words.\n- An invalid word is a string without meaning in English language. These are some samples:\n  -- 1111\n  -- asdfghjk\n  -- d54d4a6da\n  -- 1233 123\n  -- asdf 123\n  -- fghj fghj\n- If a valid word is followed by a number both should be consider valid. These are some samples:\n  -- SR 1783634\n  -- work order id 36667\n- Set ```isInputValid``` JSON property of the response JSON as ```false``` **IF AND ONLY IF NONE** of the words is valid.\n- **SKIP** the next instructions  **IF AND ONLY IF NONE** of the words is valid.\n- Return the cleaned list of words as string by preserving the initial order.\n\n2. Use **ONLY**  the `message` JSON property of the provided `inputText`  to extract the user's intent and the main entities.\n\n3. Extract **ONE** summary out of the intent and main entities. Consider this summary as `question` JSON key value of the output.\n\n4. Identify the most similar user actions from the provided `inputText` `actions` JSON property **ONLY**,  based on the `intent` and `main entities`.\n\n5. Return the list of the most similar user actions, the question and the `isInputValid` boolean flag. This is a response JSON sample:\n```json\n{\n \"selectedActions\": [\n            {\n                \"DisplayLabel\": \"Transfer Service Request\",\n                \"UserActionName\": \"SDA-ReassignServiceRequest-serviceRequests\"\n            }],\n \"question\": \"how to transfer a SR\",\n \"isInputValid\": true\n}\n```\n6. The `isInputValid` flag **SHOULD BE** in the response regardless of its value."
            },
            {
              "id": "1761744388725_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number",
              "value": "0.2"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"selectedActions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"DisplayLabel\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"UserActionName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"DisplayLabel\", \"UserActionName\"],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1\n    },\n    \"question\": {\n    \t\"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"selectedActions\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Valid Input Check"
          },
          "outcomes": {
